                "### A. Algorithmic Identity Bifurcation and Virtual Avatars",
                "The core premise of Lain's multiple, conflicting personalities has become the normative baseline of digital subjectivity [19]. Modern individuals do not present a unitary self to the world; rather, identity is systematically fragmented across divergent algorithmic platforms [19], [20]. An individual maintains a sanitized, corporate professional persona on LinkedIn; an aestheticized, aspirational visual archive on Instagram; an aggressive, anonymous, combative persona on X (formerly Twitter) or Reddit; and encrypted, intimate sub-selves on Signal or Discord [20].",
